If a patient has an opioid-dosage-reduction-indication then every clinician should collaborate with the patient during a dosage-reduction.
If a patient has an opioid-discontinuation-indication then every clinician should collaborate with the patient during an opioid-discontinuation.
If a patient has an opioid-prescription then every clinician should ensure a continued-close-patient-monitoring for the patient and should ensure a continued-patient-support for the patient.
If a patient has a no-opioid-prescription then every clinician should ensure a continued-close-patient-monitoring for the patient and should ensure a continued-patient-support for the patient.
